00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.329 align:start position:0%
 
foreign  throwing a ball up into the air the  harder you throw it the faster it  travels and the higher it goes before  falling back down if you threw it hard  enough it would actually fly away from  the earth like a rocket but what if the  Earth was condensed to the volume of a  marble no matter how hard you threw your  ball it would always fall back down to  you it could never escape this  marble-sized Earth has essentially  become a black hole a region of space  with a gravitational field so strong  that nothing not even light can escape  let's go back to when the Earth was at  its normal volume the speed that an  object must be traveling at when it  leaves the surface of the Earth is  called the Earth's escape velocity the  escape velocity of the Earth depends on  the gravitational pull that the Earth  exerts on the object that's trying to  escape gravity is an attractive force  between objects with mass the  gravitational force between two objects  depends on their mass and the distance  between their centers the greater their  masses and the shorter the distance  between each object the greater  gravitational pull one exerts on the  other and therefore the higher the  escape Velocity must be since the mass  of the earth is many times larger than  the objects we launch from it the mass  of the object is considered  insignificant and scientists only  consider the Earth's mass when  determining how fast an object like a  rocket where your ball has to go to  escape the Earth in such an estimation  the Earth's escape velocity is about 39  000 kilometers per hour roughly 50 times  faster than the average speed of an  airplane  now let's revisit our marble-sized Earth  in this scenario the Earth is smaller in  diameter but unchanged in Mass the  escape Velocity will be higher since an  object on the Earth's surface would be  much closer to its Center  if we were to continue squishing the  Earth the escape Velocity would approach  the speed of light nothing can move  faster than the speed of light so your  ball or any object for that matter could  never achieve a high enough velocity to  escape the compressed Earth this is how  the Earth would become a black hole  a hundred years ago the existence of  black holes was speculation scientists  had developed numerous theories that  used black holes as tools for  understanding the fundamental laws of  the universe like explaining the  beginning of time in this way scientists  had mathematical proof that black holes  must exist but little physical evidence  to support the theory after all how can  you see something from which no light  escapes  astrophysicists theorized that they  could Instead try to capture the  silhouette of a black hole  since black holes exert an extremely  strong gravitational pull any nearby  matter is rapidly drawn towards them  creating an accretion disk that spirals  inward the accretion disk exists just  outside of a black hole's Event Horizon  which can be thought of as the point of  no return anything that passes The Event  Horizon will be sucked in by the intense  gravity of the black hole due to  frictional heating the fast-moving  matter in the accretion disk glows  emitting light this light is bent by the  gravity of the black hole creating a  glowing ring that we can see in 2019  scientists did just that they observed a  ring of light emanating from an  accretion disk this visually confirmed  the existence of black holes for the  first time in history using an array of  eight ground-based telescopes across our  planet astrophysicists captured images  of a massive black hole at the center of  Messier 87 a Galaxy 55 million light  years from Earth this major breakthrough  served to support decades-old scientific  theories about black holes and even some  of the stories that science fiction  authors had written about them with  increasingly complex technology that  allows us to observe the depths of our  universe at higher resolution scientists  increase our understanding of cosmic  phenomena and find new questions to ask  ranging from the potential to harvest  energy from a black hole to discovering  plasma Jets streams of energy and hot  matter that spew from the center of  black holes with a gravitational force  so immense it's no wonder that  scientists can't escape the irresistible  Mysteries hidden deep within black holes  [Music]  thank you  [Music]

